      "title": "Executive Brief",
      "content": "**Key judgement.** The current surveillance picture for **Hand-Foot-Mouth Disease** is best read as a **moderate but rising signal** rather than a confirmed emergency. Over 2025-05-24 to 2026-05-23, the extract contains 30,836 cases and 0 deaths across 1 disease; the latest observation accounts for 1,477 cases.\n\n**What this means.** The immediate analytical priority is to determine whether the recent rise reflects sustained transmission, seasonal rebound, delayed reporting, or a change in ascertainment. The current evidence is count-based because rate fields are unavailable; confidence in the numeric extract is 90%, with interpretation still dependent on reporting definitions.\n\n### Analyst Readout\n- **Deterministic surveillance summary**: The report covers 1 disease, 30,836 cumulative cases, and 0 high-risk diseases. `summary:total_cases, summary:high_risk_diseases, disease:D048.risk_score, disease:D048.latest_cases, disease:D048.change_pct`",
