      "content": "### Curve Reading\nThe curve for **Hand-Foot-Mouth Disease** has turned upward in the most recent observations. The latest point is 1,477 cases, up +84.6% from the previous observation. The last 4 reporting periods account for 3,723 cases, +279.5% above the preceding 4-period window, and the peak occurs at 2026-W21 with 1,477 cases.\n\n### Interpretation\n- **Hand-Foot-Mouth Disease**: read the increase as a short-horizon pressure signal. The pattern should be checked against reporting lag, school or childcare calendars, and any age/geographic concentration if those fields become available.\n  - Last 4 periods changed +279.5% versus the preceding 4 periods.\n  - Latest value is 3.5x the pre-latest median.\n  - Peak observed period is 2026-W21 with 1,477 cases.\n\n### Anomaly Check\n- The latest point is elevated, but it does not meet the statistical anomaly threshold used here. This keeps the judgement in the “rising signal for review” category rather than an automatic alert.",
